:: Xavier Ask for Nickname [nobr]

/* This is the scene that appears when the PC asks to be called by a nickname. */
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> raises an eyebrow as you walk up and shoos away those around him. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>. What can I do for you?”</span> He gives you an intriguing smile, one that is somehow both friendly and like he is looking at a piece of meat to purchase at the market. You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> if he wouldn’t mind calling you by a nickname. Your real name is fine, and all, but since you are friends you’d rather if he called you by something else. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh? You can tell me what you’d like to be called.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> takes a step closer to you, standing almost uncomfortably close, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But I won’t guarantee I’ll use it instead of more… creative names.”</span> <br>
<br>
<div id=choice>
<<textbox "$XavierNickname" $XavierNickname>><br>
<br>
	<<link "Continue">>
	<<replace"#choice">>
        <<set $Nickname.Xavier to 1>>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$XavierNickname</span>, eh?”</span> He lets the name linger in the air for a minute, seeing how it sounds. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ll think about it. Though next time you should come to me when deciding your nicknames. I can think of many words that suit you better.”</span> He gives you a cheeky smile, though his eyes are serious. You can’t be sure if he is just messing with you or not, which is pretty classic <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>. <br>
        <br>
        <<endByLocation>>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>